diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 15eb658..b7af338 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -1,5 +1,27 @@
 # Thorch
 
+## 120 Hz presentation proof of concept
+
+The kiosk path requests `1920x1080@120Hz` on the top DSI output and forces
+Azahar's `skip_presenting_duplicate_frames` setting before every launch. Azahar
+continues to run at 100% emulation speed; the setting only prevents redundant
+presentation of unchanged frames so an external Vulkan frame-generation layer
+can see the real cadence.
+
+The `thorch-mako` package builds a pinned MAKO Renderer revision for AArch64,
+including the Vulkan layer, launcher, and CLI. `thords-azahar` is the single
+launch boundary for the real HOME Menu and all titles. It creates a private
+ThorDS MAKO profile with adaptive 120 FPS output and a 5x ceiling, then uses
+`mako-launch` automatically. If the layer is unavailable or the launch fails,
+the helper launches Azahar normally. This keeps the image bootable while the
+native renderer is being validated on the actual Thor GPU.
+
+The hidden L3+R3 chord is handled by `thords-framegen-input`. It requires both
+stick-clicks within 300 ms, ignores repeats until release, and persists the
+state in `~/.config/thords/frame-generation.state`. Development status is
+available with `thords-framegen status`; runtime diagnostics are written to
+`/var/log/thords/framegen.log`.
+
 Thorch is an experimental Arch Linux ARM image for the AYN Thor, built on top of
 public ROCKNIX work. It syncs ROCKNIX's SM8550 kernel recipe, patch stack, Thor
 DTS overlays, firmware, runtime graphics pieces, FEX assets, device
